  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A small gouache painting of a cactus with a pink and red trunk and arms in yellow, green and blue, signed crump 14, photographed on a wooden table.",
    "description": "A square gouache painting on white paper, photographed on a wooden table, with crump 14 written in the upper right. A cactus with a thick pink and red streaked trunk rises from the bottom, topped by pink horns. From it grow a yellow lobed arm at left, a green and blue spiky arm at right, a blue spiky pad at lower right, and a thin branch with small pink spines at upper left. Forms are outlined in black and filled with streaky gouache.",
    "impression": "A cactus wearing a different colour on every limb, like a plant that cannot decide what it is. The pink trunk gives it a body warmth that makes it feel like an animal. Signed and dated, so it is a finished study rather than a sketch.",
